Track 1: The Roof Answers in Fifths
- Story & Context: During an early rehearsal, Arzhan sustains a low drone while slowly changing mouth shape. One upper partial suddenly makes a loose section of metal roofing vibrate across the hall. Nia places a contact microphone on the support beam and discovers that the roof buzz arrives slightly after every concentrated overtone peak. She builds the first kick pattern around that delay rather than correcting it. Ellis shadows the overtone with pedal steel, repeatedly gliding through the exact pitch where the roof begins to answer. Sayan keeps only a low frame-drum pulse until the final section, when the electronic beat drops out and the hall resonance continues alone. The track ends not on a chord, but when Arzhan relaxes the overtone focus and the roof stops vibrating.
