Track 2: Three Heels Before the Gate
- Story & Context: Sayan notices that the old sliding gate closes properly only after someone kicks the warped wooden threshold three times. Nia records the impacts and maps them beneath a Jersey-club triplet pattern. The first two heel strikes line up with programmed kicks; the third lands late because the threshold flexes. Instead of tightening the timing, the band makes that late third impact the signature turnaround of the track. Arzhan keeps a narrow overtone melody over a low drone while Ellis plays muted pedal-steel harmonics that descend each time the gate rattles. Midway through the piece, the gate finally closes smoothly and stops producing the expected metallic answer. The musicians keep the missing space in the pattern rather than replacing it with another sound.
