Track 3: Breath Mark on the Western Felt
- Story & Context: In deep winter, condensation from Arzhan's breath begins leaving a temporary dark patch on the western felt screen whenever he turns toward it during long sustained passages. Sayan marks the position with chalk so the singer can return to the same acoustic point. Nia samples the sound difference between facing the reflective roof and facing the absorbent felt, using the contrast as a live filter transition. Ellis performs one extremely slow steel glide over thirty-two bars, moving from a bright harmonic aligned with the roof-facing voice to a darker pitch when Arzhan turns toward the felt. The final section contains almost no drums. The only pulse comes from shallow breaths, frame-drum fingertip taps, and one distant heater relay. When the condensation mark dries and disappears, the track ends.
